{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/508491-can-demons-have-non-human-covers","id":508491,"title":"Can Demons have non-human Covers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-08T15:32:21-07:00","id":508491,"title":"Can Demons have non-human Covers?","content":"Let's say I want to make a soul pact with a changeling, but I want my resulting Cover to be able to switch between the changeling's Mien And Mask. Would that work? Also, I assume only beings with souls or altered souls can make soul pacts, so Pandorans, Abyssals, True Fae and the like are out, right?<br /> <br /> Also, could I have a vehicle with a holographic driver as my Cover, Transformers style? If so, how do I do that?<br /> <br /> Can I have a mundane animal as a Cover? Do I keep my Mental/Social stats but use the Physical stats of the animal? Can I still speak (I am sure I'd have to roll compromise if I could)? If so, how do I do that?<br /> <br /> And in all those previous cases, would my Embeds and Exploits still work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-08-2015, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T15:45:03-07:00","id":508515,"title":"","content":"You can have supernatural creatures enter soul pacts but you end up with a copy of their human if you cash it in; you don't get their powers.<br /> <br /> Yes, you can be a vehicle but doing anything that the vehcile wouldn't normally do would be a Cover violation. I think the book specifically mentions that Demons don't do animal or material covers, as a general rule, because it's really hard to do anything at all while maintaining such a Cover.<br /> <br /> Yes, your powers would still work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T16:28:59-07:00","id":508543,"title":"","content":"Yes you could but you would take damage from cashing in a non human soul pact but once you do it would be effectively human. You would require deep cover and/or show of power to seem more like the template in question.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T18:43:17-07:00","id":508615,"title":"","content":"The supernatural stuff has already been covered, so I'll skip that. I recall reading somewhere that part of the reason animals are avoided is because they tend to also be extremely weak covers and the restrictions being a cat brings aren't worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T19:46:06-07:00","id":508644,"title":"","content":"Well actually the deal is that it's rather hard to enter soul pacts with inanimate objects and animals, so demons with such covers either fell with them as their original cover, or angel-jacked the wrong angel. <br /> <br /> That said, that exploit that allows a demon to take urban legends as temporary covers could result in some unusual covers- urban legends cover a lot of ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T14:53:35-07:00","id":511178,"title":"","content":"The other problem with animal Covers is that animals can't sign Pacts, meaning that in order to get one you'd need to angel-jack it. And if you're going through the trouble and risk of angel-jacking, you usually want more out of it than a 1 or 2 dot Cover of some alley cat. <br /> <br /> I'd imagine that you'd keep your same stats as normal, though actually using them may be problematic and compromise-inducing, depending on what you're doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T14:55:18-07:00","id":511181,"title":"","content":"Haven't Changelings had their souls effectively shredded? I'd think that between the Thorns and the existence of their fetch, there isn't enough soul left to sell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T15:54:19-07:00","id":511268,"title":"","content":"I had a player start with a second cover of a dog. Their main cover was homeless and the dog was a stray, so that helped with some of the cover breaking logistics of it. I ruled they couldn't speak as the dog because they lacked the correct mouth parts.<br /> <br /> You keep the same physical stats the same you would with any other cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T08:33:46-07:00","id":512011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/508491-can-demons-have-non-human-covers?p=511181#post511181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't Changelings had their souls effectively shredded? I'd think that between the Thorns and the existence of their fetch, there isn't enough soul left to sell.</div> </div> </div> </div> In 1e at least, the Lost regained their soul upon returning to reality, though changed. The only PC supernatural template that may count as effectively soulless for the purpose of pacts is a promethean. Others have pointed out that you can only take the personal connections and human appearance, not powers - that said, there are a couple of abilities demons can learn (Deep Cover and Show of Power) that allow them to mimic being a supernatural.<br /> <br /> <br /> Demons can absolutely take animal forms. There are exploits for taking cars and houses, as well as spiritual beings, as Covers as well. Animals stand out as being the hardest to really gain as a Cover, but you can start as one, and shore it up at least; very difficult to get a new one. Still possible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T14:03:31-07:00","id":512298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/508491-can-demons-have-non-human-covers?p=511181#post511181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't Changelings had their souls effectively shredded? I'd think that between the Thorns and the existence of their fetch, there isn't enough soul left to sell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually they define what constitutes a soul vis-\u00e0-vis the unchained and contracts. Essentially a soul is all the things that constitute a distinguishable identity. Thus why the effect of a soul pact is stepping into a person's life and acquiring all non-memory related things to the person. The core book mentions the metaphysical soul being obliterated I think, but ironically I don't think it is actually required for a being to posses a soul to be targeted by a soul pact. So Changelings are viable targets for a soul pact as long as they remain identifiable as individuals.They are just not favored targets because the supernatural burn that occurs when you use a soul pact on any supernatural being; plus the whole being hunted by a supernatural monster will probably stick anyway and demon's have enough problems with the GM that I doubt many are eager to add a member of the Sidhe to the list of things to watch out for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 05-13-2015, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T19:58:02-07:00","id":512492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/508491-can-demons-have-non-human-covers?p=512011#post512011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In 1e at least, the Lost regained their soul upon returning to reality, though changed. The only PC supernatural template that may count as effectively soulless for the purpose of pacts is a promethean. Others have pointed out that you can only take the personal connections and human appearance, not powers - that said, there are a couple of abilities demons can learn (Deep Cover and Show of Power) that allow them to mimic being a supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually it's ambiguous if changelings have souls, in the crossover rules for mages and changelings it mentions that mages can't tell if changelings have souls or not- They have something there, but it may not be a soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T05:39:20-07:00","id":512840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/508491-can-demons-have-non-human-covers?p=512492#post512492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually it's ambiguous if changelings have souls, in the crossover rules for mages and changelings it mentions that mages can't tell if changelings have souls or not- They have something there, but it may not be a soul.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its ambiguous if they have the supernal spark as mages define it; not a surprise, considering mages have trouble dealing with any form supernatural soul. Awakened magic is better at finding mysteries to solve than giving pure answers. As such, we know that the Lost do have SOMETHING there (that side section you refer to admits it), and that something is enough of a soul for demons to interact with via pact. That entire ambiguity is meant to leave the question open so there's no definite answer - having the soul pact fail would give a very definite answer. <br /> <br /> Furthermore, Soulless is a specific condition in 2e. We don't know about 2e Lost, but there's a good chance they won't suffer from that effect as a whole, but possibly may suffer from it through other effects like the Thorns. Changelings might not be human, but they aren't highly susceptable to possession, and don't have reversed Virtue/Vices. I see no reason to assume they can't be pacted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T00:39:17-07:00","id":596582,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, I think I have to weigh in on the soul issue, from the point of view of my-clerical-aspirant-self;<br /> <br /> The soul-concept most commonly referred to in most WoD books, and in most of western literature, is the Cartesian Soul, while the soul-concept used in Demon is apparently the Narrativist Soul. These are distinct concepts. <br /> <br /> The Cartesian Soul is what most people mean when they say 'soul'; a supernatural object which is naturally attached to an individual by some vague means. This is the kind of soul that can be stolen by a mage, and which Prometheans lack. It is the soul-concept predominant in modern Christianity, modern Judaism, and ancient Islam (there is theological debate within Islam as to the applicability of the Cartesian concept, as it applies inconsistently in faqi, which is Islamic jurisprudence). It is <u>not</u> the source of an individual's identity in the Abrahamic religions. Nor in WoD is it the source of identify, as demonstrated by the fact that a soul-less individual does not cease to be recognizable, and Prometheans still have an identity. Animals are not supposed to have Cartesian Souls according to most theologies that use the concept (with the notable exceptions of Norse paganism and Egyptian paganism [partially, as animals in Egyptian paganism do not possess all of the soul-parts humans do]). I'm reasonably certain that it says somewhere in some of the WoD books that animals don't have souls (not that I can name one at the moment). It seems reasonable to assume they mean the Cartesian Soul. <br /> <br /> The Narrativist Soul is a metaphysical abstract, as opposed to a supernatural object. It is synonymous with identity, and thus it is the soul that Demon appears to use. The Narrativist Soul is the soul-concept used in Buddhism (see the Doctrine of The Carriage), and as a non-supernatural concept of the soul it is endorsed by some groups and individuals that endorse an anti-supernatural understanding of the world. Richard Dawkins refers to it in his TED Talk &quot;Our Queer Universe&quot;. The Narrativist Soul is something shared by everything that has an identity, so animals and buildings have it as well. <br /> <br /> What all that boils down to is that it is easiest to work out how soul-issues work if you just realize the word 'soul' means one thing in one place and another thing in another place. In other words you can barter with a Mage for the (Cartesian) soul he has stolen, but you can't use it for Cover, because it's not the same thing as what you build cover out of (identity). Likewise, if you find a mortal who is missing his (Cartesian) soul, you can still make a soul-pact with him for his (Narrativist) Soul. Ditto for Prometheans. It also means you can totally make a soul-pact with an ape for his soul, provided he knows sign language, and you teach him to sign his name first. Both of those sound like options for really patient demons.<br /> <br /> In theory, you could make soul-pacts with any animal you could communicate significantly with, provided they could write in some limited capacity. Since many beings in the WoD can communicate with animals, you could make pacts with them provided you had some help. Also consider that writing may not be as big a limitation as one might think, since there is no qualifier for the quality of the writing. If your dog puts a paw print on the paper, it might count.<br /> <br /> As far as inanimate objects, well, is there anything in the WoD that can talk to them? I tend to think there might be. Many machines could produce some kind of writing or other self-identifier. Their blood might be a limiting factor, but their is no real definition given for blood either. I would generally say that any fluid vital to the operation of the machine qualifies. <br /> <br /> And yeah, the Cover rating would be low, but I could see some advantages to these crazy covers; In dog-form, you can get away with a lot just using Cause And Effect, or imagine you take the soul of the printer/fax/copier located in an office-building infrastructure. Every document they print, you send an identical fax to your local Agency. Even with a low Cover, who is actually going to accuse the printer of being the Mole?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1547-bunnirabbi","name":"BunniRabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1547_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:26:53-07:00","id":597091,"title":"","content":"Actually, the nature of the Changeling\u00b4s soul, or any other supernatural for that matter isn\u00b4t relevant. What the Demon is actually buying is the &quot;life&quot; of the signer, not the spiritual stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T13:32:05-07:00","id":597212,"title":"","content":"Yes and demon can take a non human cover. They can take on vampire cover but they won't have all the powers and stuff so they will stand out more. Then again that is the show of power exploit is for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T14:19:53-07:00","id":597314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BunniRabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/508491-can-demons-have-non-human-covers?p=596582#post596582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, I think I have to weigh in on the soul issue, from the point of view of my-clerical-aspirant-self;<br /> <br /> The soul-concept most commonly referred to in most WoD books, and in most of western literature, is the Cartesian Soul, while the soul-concept used in Demon is apparently the Narrativist Soul. These are distinct concepts.<br /> <br /> The Cartesian Soul is what most people mean when they say 'soul'; a supernatural object which is naturally attached to an individual by some vague means. This is the kind of soul that can be stolen by a mage, and which Prometheans lack. It is the soul-concept predominant in modern Christianity, modern Judaism, and ancient Islam (there is theological debate within Islam as to the applicability of the Cartesian concept, as it applies inconsistently in faqi, which is Islamic jurisprudence). It is <u>not</u> the source of an individual's identity in the Abrahamic religions. Nor in WoD is it the source of identify, as demonstrated by the fact that a soul-less individual does not cease to be recognizable, and Prometheans still have an identity. Animals are not supposed to have Cartesian Souls according to most theologies that use the concept (with the notable exceptions of Norse paganism and Egyptian paganism [partially, as animals in Egyptian paganism do not possess all of the soul-parts humans do]). I'm reasonably certain that it says somewhere in some of the WoD books that animals don't have souls (not that I can name one at the moment). It seems reasonable to assume they mean the Cartesian Soul.<br /> <br /> The Narrativist Soul is a metaphysical abstract, as opposed to a supernatural object. It is synonymous with identity, and thus it is the soul that Demon appears to use. The Narrativist Soul is the soul-concept used in Buddhism (see the Doctrine of The Carriage), and as a non-supernatural concept of the soul it is endorsed by some groups and individuals that endorse an anti-supernatural understanding of the world. Richard Dawkins refers to it in his TED Talk &quot;Our Queer Universe&quot;. The Narrativist Soul is something shared by everything that has an identity, so animals and buildings have it as well.<br /> <br /> What all that boils down to is that it is easiest to work out how soul-issues work if you just realize the word 'soul' means one thing in one place and another thing in another place. In other words you can barter with a Mage for the (Cartesian) soul he has stolen, but you can't use it for Cover, because it's not the same thing as what you build cover out of (identity). Likewise, if you find a mortal who is missing his (Cartesian) soul, you can still make a soul-pact with him for his (Narrativist) Soul. Ditto for Prometheans. It also means you can totally make a soul-pact with an ape for his soul, provided he knows sign language, and you teach him to sign his name first. Both of those sound like options for really patient demons.<br /> <br /> In theory, you could make soul-pacts with any animal you could communicate significantly with, provided they could write in some limited capacity. Since many beings in the WoD can communicate with animals, you could make pacts with them provided you had some help. Also consider that writing may not be as big a limitation as one might think, since there is no qualifier for the quality of the writing. If your dog puts a paw print on the paper, it might count.<br /> <br /> As far as inanimate objects, well, is there anything in the WoD that can talk to them? I tend to think there might be. Many machines could produce some kind of writing or other self-identifier. Their blood might be a limiting factor, but their is no real definition given for blood either. I would generally say that any fluid vital to the operation of the machine qualifies.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the Cover rating would be low, but I could see some advantages to these crazy covers; In dog-form, you can get away with a lot just using Cause And Effect, or imagine you take the soul of the printer/fax/copier located in an office-building infrastructure. Every document they print, you send an identical fax to your local Agency. Even with a low Cover, who is actually going to accuse the printer of being the Mole?</div> </div> </div> </div> This is easily one of the most informative and interesting posts I've read online in a long while, BunniRabbi. You deserve a Like not only for opening my eyes, but for also inspiring new ideas for my games. Keep it up and you'll be an amazing cleric.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T15:12:43-07:00","id":599858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BunniRabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/508491-can-demons-have-non-human-covers?p=596582#post596582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In theory, you could make soul-pacts with any animal you could communicate significantly with, provided they could write in some limited capacity. Since many beings in the WoD can communicate with animals, you could make pacts with them provided you had some help. Also consider that writing may not be as big a limitation as one might think, since there is no qualifier for the quality of the writing. If your dog puts a paw print on the paper, it might count.</div> </div> </div> </div>Suddenly, Animal Ken has a lot more value...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/405-ragecryx","name":"ragecryx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar405_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}